// HAMLET ACHIEVEMENT POINTS - what each achievement is worth, and what every key in this file does.
// This file is yours. Hamlet reads it each time the achievements window opens and never writes to
// it. The first time there is no copy in %AppData%\Hamlet\achievements\, this one is copied there,
// and that copy is never replaced afterward. Lines that start with // are notes and are skipped.
// If the file cannot be read, the page says so and shows no scores rather than made-up ones.
//
// TOP-LEVEL KEYS
//   "_about"        One line of prose about the file.
//   "continents"    A first contact on each of the seven continents.
//   "countries"     One for each DXCC entity worked.
//   "states"        One for each US state worked, read from the STATE field of the log record.
//                   It scores only on a United States, Alaska or Hawaii record, and only as one of
//                   the fifty two-letter codes, so DC, a Canadian province and a blank score
//                   nothing. Hamlet never works out a state from a callsign.
//   "grids"         One for each four-character grid square worked.
//   "total_miles"   Every logged mile, grid to grid, added up.
//   "bands"         A first contact on each band.
//   "modes"         A first contact in each mode.
//   "hall_of_fame"  Once-only firsts. Each key inside it is one first, with its points:
//     "first_contact"           your first logged contact
//     "first_dx"                your first contact in a DXCC entity other than your own (Hamlet
//                               takes your own to be the entity of the first record in the log)
//     "first_psk31"             your first PSK31 contact
//     "first_olivia"            your first Olivia contact
//     "first_cw_qso"            your first Morse (CW) contact
//     "first_over_5000_miles"   your first contact 5,000 miles or more away
//     "first_over_10000_miles"  your first contact 10,000 miles or more away
//     "first_answer_to_own_cq"  a station answering your own CQ; a log cannot show who called
//                               first, so Hamlet never awards this one
//   "ranks"         The running totals where each rank begins, lowest first. Below the first one
//                   you are Rank 1, and passing each one moves you up a rank.
//   "levels"        For each kind, the counts where Bronze, Silver, Gold and Platinum begin, lowest
//                   first; for "total_miles" they are miles. A kind with more than four shows
//                   Level 5 and up past Platinum.
//   "rank_names"    Empty as shipped, so every rank shows Rank n. Put your names for your ranks in
//                   it, Rank 1 first, for example  "rank_names": ["Listener", "Novice", "Operator"],
//                   A shorter list names the first ranks and the rest show Rank n. Anything other
//                   than a list of names is ignored, and every rank shows Rank n.
//
// KEYS INSIDE A KIND
//   "per"           Points for each one worked. Under "continents" it is a table of points by
//                   continent: "NA" North America, "SA" South America, "EU" Europe, "AF" Africa,
//                   "AS" Asia, "OC" Oceania, "AN" Antarctica.
//   "special"       Named ones worth something other than "per": a band such as "160m", a mode
//                   such as "CW", or a state such as "AK". A special replaces "per"; it is not
//                   added to it.
//   "all"           A bonus for working every one: all seven continents, all fifty states, every
//                   HF band Hamlet lists, or every mode a contact can be made in.
//   "milestones"    Bonuses at a count worked. "10": 25 means 25 more points once you reach ten.
//   "tiers"         The same shape, for "total_miles". "50000": 5 means 5 points once your miles
//                   reach 50,000.
